@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxProgress))]
@attribute [Route("/components/" + nameof(HxProgressBar))]

<ApiDoc Type="typeof(HxProgress)">
    <DocHeading Title="Basic usage" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Bar sizing" />

    <DocHeading Title="Width" Level="4" />
    <p>
        The width of each progress bar is set by its <code>Value</code> (normalized according to <code>MinValue</code> and <code>MaxValue</code>, see <a href="#scale">Scale</a>).
        The width of the whole progress (the track) follows its container; use the <code>CssClass</code> parameter
        with the <a href="https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/width/">width utilities</a> (e.g. <code>w-50</code>) to change it.
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Width)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Height" Level="4" />
    <p>Use the <code>Height</code> parameter (in pixels) to set the height of the progress; the inner progress bars resize accordingly.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Height)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Labels" />
    <p>Use the <code>Label</code> parameter (or the child content) to place a text label on the progress bar.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Labels)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Long labels" Level="4" />
    <p>
        By default, the content of the progress bar is clipped (<code>overflow: hidden</code>), so it does not bleed out of the bar.
        If the progress bar is shorter than its label, the label is capped and may become unreadable.
        To change this behavior, add the <code>overflow-visible</code> CSS class (using the <code>CssClass</code> parameter),
        together with a text color which is readable on both the bar and the track (e.g. <code>fg-body</code>).
    </p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_LongLabels)" Tabs="false" />
    <DocAlert Type="DocAlertType.Warning">
        Labels longer than the progress bar may not be fully accessible this way, because the text color needs a sufficient contrast ratio
        with both the progress bar and the track background colors. If the text can overlap the progress bar, consider displaying the label outside of the progress bar.
    </DocAlert>

    <DocHeading Title="Backgrounds" />
    <p>The <code>Color</code> parameter renders the <code>theme-*</code> class, which sets both the fill color and a contrasting label color.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Backgrounds)" />

    <DocHeading Title="MultipleBars" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_MultipleBars)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Striped" />
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Striped)" />

    <DocHeading Title="Animated stripes" />
    <p>When the parameter <code>HxProgressBar.Animated</code> is set to <code>true</code>, stripes are automatically enabled and animated.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_AnimatedStripes)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Setting parameters" />
    <p>Some parameters can be set for all progress bars at once on the <code>HxProgress</code> component. Inherited values can be overridden on the child components.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_SettingParameters)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Scale" />
    <p>You can set a scale for the progress bar, for example from <code>-100</code> to <code>100</code> as shown below. Supplied values are normalized according to the <code>MinValue</code> and <code>MaxValue</code> set. The default values are <code>0</code> and <code>100</code>.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Scales)" Tabs="false" />

    <DocHeading Title="Interactive" />
    <p>The progress value can be easily changed at runtime. When that occurs, the progress bar updates with an animation.</p>
    <Demo Type="typeof(HxProgress_Demo_Interactive)" />
</ApiDoc>

